' @guidance:
' Create or update the PlantUML diagram describing how files tagged with the
' @guidance marker are processed. This is a SEPARATE way of using Ghostwriter
' and is NOT part of the Act/episode functionality.
'
' - Implemented by GuidanceProcessor (extends AIFileProcessor, NOT ActProcessor).
' - Reuses the generic project traversal (module discovery, recursion, match()
'   filtering) but does NOT run Act episodes.
' - Show per-file handling: reviewer lookup by extension, guidance extraction via
'   the @guidance: marker, and the decision logic (guidance found / skip).
' - Show prompt composition, provider dispatch, and the report (getReport())
'   which is distinct from the Act pipeline getResults().
' - Keep the diagram readable; prefer clear partitions/swimlanes over clutter.

@startuml
title Ghostwriter - @guidance Tag File Processing (standalone mode, not an Act)

skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #F5F7FA
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #4A6FA5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF3CD
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #EDF7ED
skinparam PartitionBorderColor #999999

|#E8EEF7|GuidanceProcessor|
start
:Construct GuidanceProcessor
(extends AIFileProcessor, not ActProcessor);
:Load reviewers with ServiceLoader<Reviewer>;
:Index reviewers by normalized file extension;

|#E8EEF7|AbstractFileProcessor traversal|
:scanFolder(projectDir) creates ProjectLayout;
if (nonRecursive enabled?) then (yes)
  :Skip module discovery;
else (no)
  :Discover ProjectLayout.getModules();
  :Process relevant modules serially or with
  the configured worker count;
  note right
    Each module re-enters scanFolder(). GuidanceProcessor's
    processModule() recurses into all modules when no scan
    path is set; otherwise the module must match or contain
    the configured scan path. No Act episodes are run.
  end note
endif

|#EDF3EC|GuidanceProcessor.processParentFiles|
:List children with projectLayout.listFiles(projectDir);
if (child list null or empty?) then (yes)
  :Fall back to projectDir.listFiles()
  (immediate children, or an empty list);
endif
:Remove module directories and children that do not match();
while (more eligible children?) is (yes)
  :Take next eligible child;
  |#FDF3E7|GuidanceProcessor.processFile|
  if (match(file, projectLayout)?) then (yes)
    :For regular files, look up the Reviewer
    by file extension;
    if (Reviewer available?) then (yes)
      :guidance = reviewer.perform(projectDir, file);
      note right
        The extension-specific Reviewer extracts supported
        @guidance: comment content, or returns null. The
        processor does not alter the marker in the source.
      end note
    else (no)
      :guidance = null (unsupported type
      or non-regular file);
    endif

    if (guidance found?) then (yes)
      :Choose guidance_rules and extracted guidance;
    else (no)
      if (default prompt configured?) then (yes)
        :Choose default prompt (without guidance_rules);
      else (no)
        :Skip file;
      endif
    endif

    if (guidance or default prompt selected?) then (yes)
      |#EDF7ED|AIFileProcessor / provider|
      :Use guidance system instructions
      (including configured user instructions)
      and the selected prompts;
      :Extract YAML front matter (gw.model,
      enabledTools); resolve public substitutions
      and prompt includes; configure tools;
      :Send system instructions, getProcessInfo()
      (file path, OS, and non-interactive instruction),
      and selected prompts to configured GenAI provider;
      :Execute provider.perform() (no Act episodes);
      :Return provider output;

      |#FDF3E7|GuidanceProcessor.processFile|
      :Normalize blank output to OK and increment
      the processed-file count;
      :Log output and record { file, message }
      in getReport();
    endif
  else (no)
    :Skip child;
  endif
  |#EDF3EC|GuidanceProcessor.processParentFiles|
endwhile (no)

if (project directory matches and default prompt configured?) then (yes)
  |#EDF7ED|AIFileProcessor / provider|
  :Process project directory with guidance_rules
  and default prompt using the public process(...) overload;
  :Return provider output and add a getReport() entry;
  |#EDF3EC|GuidanceProcessor.processParentFiles|
  :Log nonblank output;
else (no)
  :No folder-level fallback;
endif

|#E8EEF7|GuidanceProcessor|
:getReport() returns guidance-mode report entries,
separate from ActProcessor.getResults();
stop

legend right
  @guidance tag processing (standalone mode):
  * NOT part of Act/episode functionality; GuidanceProcessor
    extends AIFileProcessor, not ActProcessor.
  * Instructions live INSIDE the file as a "@guidance:" comment
    (constant GUIDANCE_TAG_NAME); the marker must remain unchanged
    so runs stay idempotent/repeatable.
  * Reviewers (ServiceLoader) extract guidance by file extension.
  * Per file: guidance found -> dispatch;
    no guidance -> default prompt when configured; otherwise skip.
  * getReport() is separate from ActProcessor.getResults().
endlegend

@enduml
